 "root_cause": "Model skill tools queried captured catalog/history and committed usage outside one complete service owner. Activate/view owned only their nested get, so cancelling the outer waiter could abandon the following activation commit or leave a committed-but-undelivered activation unowned; first queries also bypassed closed/full admission.",
 "changes": [
  "Own each skills_list/skill_history/skill_activate/skill_view request once from first catalog lookup through result construction and final usage registration",
  "Keep close/full checks ahead of first I/O under the existing eight admissions/two slots and shield admitted work across request or close-waiter cancellation",
  "Extract the unchanged verified get body into an already-admitted internal helper; standalone public get retains its own admission and tool reads do not recursively acquire a second slot",
  "Preserve captured revision, path/file checks, exact model JSON, history shape, final skill_activate_run authority and special revoked-error propagation",
  "Keep write-tool approval/commit logic, parser, lifecycle coordinator, budgets and all public signatures unchanged"
 ],
